1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Josefwas involved in municipal affairs, in his younger years did a lot of silversmithing and was skilled at various other jobs. He worked with, among other things, a seeding machine, and a navar, to drill water spr
2 CONC ings, which are now in the museum at Mølster. Brita was a good missionary friend and was the first to give money to an orphanage in Voss. Josef died in 1876 and Brita in 1906. They had children: Anna b. 1844, b. 1868 m. Nils Larss
2 CONC on Finnesteigen, Lars b. 1845, b. 1870 m. Ingjerd Josefsdr. Lid, Gudve b. 1848, m. Nils Davidson Gjerdåk på Løno, Steffa b. 1851, died in America, Maria b. 1855, m. m. Olav Gitleson Opeland på Øvre Lid, Brita b. 1858, died unmarri
2 CONC ed 1906, Olav b. 1861, Nils b. 1864.
