2 CONC Hordaland, Norway on April 12, 1864.  Their date and port of arrival in America is not recorded.  After arriving in America, the family lived in Winneshiek county, Iowa for about two years.  Lars Davidson homesteaded a 160-acre fa
2 CONC rm located in Mansfield Township, Freeborn county, Minnesota, about 3½ miles west of Emmons on the north side of State Line Road.  The family moved onto the Davidson Homestead in May 1866. Lars and Guri lived on the homestead for 
2 CONC the remainder of their lives.
