1 NOTE (OBIT)  Edmund Edmundson, 87, was born January 13, 1871 in Voss, Norway and passed away July 22, 1958 at the Wesley Hospital in Wadena.    He immigrated from Norway to America at the age of 21 and worked in Illinois 7 years, Madis
2 CONC on, Wisconsin 3 years, and Williamsburg, Virginia for 11 years.     He was united in marriage to Hilda Skaro, April 21, 1911 at Williamsburg, Virginia and had been married 47 years at the time of his death.  Mr. and Mrs. Edmundson
2 CONC  moved to Sebeka 45 years ago and were engaged in farming until three years ago when they moved to a home in Sebeka.     He leaves to mourn his passing his wife, three sons and three daughters, namely: Earl of Sebeka, MN; Albert, 
2 CONC New Philadelphia, OH; Blaine, Anoka, MN; Mrs. Jack Morgan (Julia), Minneapolis, MN; Mrs. Chester Tollefson (Gladys), Anoka, MN; and Mrs. Harry S. Dobble (Allene), LaGrange, IL; also Mrs. Thomas Ellefson (sister), Mt. Horeb, WI; on
2 CONC e sister, Gertrude and other relatives living in Norway, sixteen grandchildren and a host of friends.     He was a member of the Bethlehem Lutheran church in Sebeka.     Funeral services for this respected pioneer citizen were hel
2 CONC d Friday, July 25 at Bethlehem Lutheran church with Rev. R. E. Anderson officiating.
2 CONT      Mrs. Russell Nelson and Mrs. Oray Tangen sang "Face to Face" and "Nearer My God to Thee".
2 CONT      Pallbearers were Steven Niska, Wayne Kiser, John Hepola, Harry Lilliquist, John Lilliquist, Benjamin School, Fred Thompson, John Quale and Rudolph Stelck.
2 CONT      Friends and relatives attending from a distance were Albert Edmundson, New Philadelphia, Ohio; Mr. and Mrs Jack Morgan and family of Minneapolis; Mrs. and Mrs. Chester Tollefson and family of Anoka; Theodore Tollefson of Gayl
2 CONC ord, Minn; Mrs. and Mrs. Marcus Nordwall of Park Rapids; Mrs. Harry S. Dobble, LaGrange, IL; Mr. and Mrs. Blaine Edmundson of Anoka; Mrs. and Mrs. Ralph Heern, Wadena; Mr. and Mrs. Harold Broker, Verndale and Mr and Mrs. Martin He
2 CONC ern, Staples;
2 CONT      Mrs. Henry Westby and Mrs. and Mrs. Leonard Hacking, Effie, MN; Mrs. Clara Berg, Mr. Theodore Tollefson, and Mr. and Mrs. Kenneth Tollefson, all of Gaylord, MN.
2 CONT      Mrs. Herman Zimmermann of Parkers Prairie, MN, and Mr. and Mrs. A. E. Anderson of Park Rapids, MN.
