1 NAME Henry Gerhard /Stensland/
2 GIVN Henry Gerhard
2 SURN Stensland
2 _MARNM Stensland
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mabel
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 SEP 1882
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint Thomas
3 STAE North Dakota
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 MAR 1975
2 PLAC Nursing Home
2 ADDR
3 CITY Strum
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Everyone that knew him had good feelings about him. Easy going, honest and hard working but not a good business man.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blue eyes, brown hair. Thin, medium build. Easy smile and laugh. I never saw him angry.
2 CONT
2 CONT After he married Nora they lived with Lauritz and Maria Bye - Nora’s parents with their son Alden and Maria’s granddaughter Mary Louise Strehlow (according to the 1940 census). During the depression he read “Gone With the Wind” al
2 CONC oud to the family for evening entertainment. They had no money for movies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Worked for his brother-in-law Clarence Bye at Clarence’s dairy farm for a number of years. Then he ran the feed mill in Osseo, Wisconsin for several years before retiring.
2 CONT
2 CONT “Henrik Steensland” was confirmed at Mabel First Lutheran by Pastor A. O. Langehough in class of 1897. 
1 FAMC @F4029352249270011189@
1 FAMS @F6000000026341677834@
1 RFN geni:6000000026341677829
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/92/2c/af/2d/5344483b50d3e257/henry_stensland_oval_original.jpg?hash=7f396b9fe09e251b9a3c53a6a04ef18618e3ae0f9e6365efdcf6406c68053331.1794988799
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE
2 CONT Mabel Record - March 29, 1975 - Funeral services were conducted at 11 a.m. Tuesday, March 18, 1975 at the Evangelical Lutheran Church in Osseo, WI for Henry Stensland, 92, former Mabel man who died Saturday March 15, 1975 at a nur
2 CONC sing home in Strum, WI.  The Rev. H. P. Walker officiated. Burial was in the Mabel Cemetery.  He was born September 30, 1882 at St. Thomas, SD, the son of Elias and Ingebor (Nelson) Stensland.  He came to Mabel when a child and li
2 CONC ved here until 1943, when he moved to Osseo.  He was engaged as a livestock buyer and operator of the Mabel Feed Mill with B. E. Rasmus and also clerked for several years at the E. A. Halverson grocery store.
2 CONT On March 19, 1919, he married Leonora Bye of Mabel.  Survivors are his wife; one son, Alden, Richmond, VA; two grandchildren, Mark Stensland, Minneapolis; Susan Stensland, Harrisonburg, VA; one brother, Leonard, Mabel, MN and a si
2 CONC ster, Mrs. Harry (Inga) Eckert, Sioux Falls, SD. Four sisters and three brothers preceded him in death.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 18 MAR 2015
3 TIME 13:57:59
