1 NOTE The church records for Voss show that Niels Knudsen Mørqve, age 24 and unmarried, left for northern Norway on the 1st of June, 1839, along with Ole Nielsen Mørqve, age 37, his wife Inger Pedersdatter Mørqve, 36, and their son, Lar
2 CONC s Olsen Mørqve, age 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Geneva Knutson, Nils lived in Hammerfest for a time before emigrating to America.  The family bible (Calvin Knutson, Tuttle, ND) reveals Nils & his family came to Capron, IL, where the Fely family lived. Nils' family 
2 CONC moved to Worth County, IA and Guri married Elling Fely in 1871. Both Nils and Elling purchased land in section 36, Hartland township, Worth County, IA in November of 1874. Elling's father, Ole, got land there in 1866. Nils and Mar
2 CONC tha Morkve joined So. Shell Rock Church in 1880.   When daughter Guri died in 1894, they helped Elling with his family.
