1 NAME Ida Leonora "Nora" /Bye/
2 GIVN Ida Leonora "Nora"
2 SURN Bye
2 _MARNM Bye
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 APR 1892
2 PLAC Spring Grove, MN
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 OCT 1978
2 PLAC Lutheran Hosp. La X, Services Osseo, WI, buried Mabel Cem
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was an excellent cook.  She made and decorated wedding cakes, and birthday cakes for hundreds of people. Always had fresh cookies and cake available in quantity when you visited her home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Was an artist in her own right. She was well known for her small dolls from pipe cleaners with hand knitted Norwegian costumes.  They were sold throughout the midwest for many years. She made dancing dolls this way, each hanging b
2 CONC y a thread from a nail and they would twirl around each other. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Very staunch Lutheran. Punished me as a boy for using “Gosh or darn” calling them swear words.
1 FAMC @F6000000012441565682@
1 FAMS @F6000000026341677834@
1 RFN geni:6000000026341190657
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/3b/70/c1/34/5344483b50c8f190/leonora_henry_stensland_1919_original.jpg?hash=77c142fe51f022223fc4fd5045d809c5dc1c6e0662d7a31b64331706f78bafea.1794988799
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE
2 CONT Funeral Services were conducted Friday at 11 a.m. at the Evangelical Luthran Church in Osseo, Wisconsin for Mrs. Leonora Stensland, 86 who died Monday October 2, 1978 at Lutheran Hospital in La Crosse. The Rev. Harry Walker and Re
2 CONC v. Jerry Kuehn officiated.  Burial was in the Mabel cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The former Leonora Bye, she was born April 12, 1892 at Spring Grove, Minnesota the daughter of Lauritz and Maria Bergrud Bye.  She graduated from the Mabel High School.
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 19, 1919, she married Henry Stensland.  They lived at Mabel until 1944 when they moved to Osseo.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by one son, Alden, Richmond, VA; two grandchildren; two great-grandchildren; two sisters, Mrs. Ruby Rasmus, Mabel and Mrs. Inga Strehlow, West St. Paul, Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband and two brothers preceded her in death.  The Mengis Funeral Home was in charge of arrangements.
