1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/188449728/kenneth-arnold-anderson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth (Swede) Anderson was 81 when he passed away peacefully at Providence St. Peter Hospital, Olympia, December 18, 2004 at 12:12 p.m. He will be missed by many of us.
2 CONT “GOD BLESS HIS SOUL”
2 CONT Kenneth was born May 12, 1923 in Plentywood, Montana to Arnold B. and Hazel I. Anderson. Ken and his dad built the “BLUE MOON TAVERN” in Plentywood, which became the most popular club in town. Ken met Elaine H. Belisle from Medici
2 CONC ne Lake, Montana in the early 40’s. They were married in 1943. Together, Ken and Elaine boast of 8 wonderful children, 22 grandchildren and many great-grandchildren and still counting.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ken was remarried to a wonderful woman, Martha, in Montana. They moved to the Olympia, Washington area in 1978 and settled in the Nisqually Valley. Martha passed in 1984 and Ken has kept the homestead going.
