1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55601522/margaret-annetta-nelson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral for Margaret Nelson, 81 of Lanesboro, will be at 11 a.m. Saturday, July 31, 2010, at United Methodist Church in Lanesboro, with Rev. Amanda Larsen and Rev. Michael Smith officiating. Burial will be in the Lanesboro Cem
2 CONC etery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret died Sunday, July 25, 2010, at Good Shepherd Lutheran Home in Rushford, where she resided since January 2009.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Annetta Nelson was born on June 17, 1929, in Lanesboro to Willie and Bertha (Gates) Nelson. She graduated from Lanesboro High School. She was a lifetime Lanesboro resident.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret worked at the IGA Grocery Store in Lanesboro from 1950 until 1976, then at Rushford Products until she retired. She was a member of the United Methodist Church, and a former Sunday School Teacher and church custodian. She
2 CONC  also belonged to the Sunshine Club, was a lifetime VFW Auxiliary member, and a member of the Legion Auxiliary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret love to play Canasta and make pies and cookies. She collected elephants and Santa Clauses, and was a serious collector of pop cans for the youth. She was also involved in Poppy sales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include one brother, Robert (Marlene) Nelson of Watford City, North Dakota; five sisters, Ruth (Jim) Ostrem and Mary Mindrum, both of Lanesboro, Jean Bremseth of Houston, Lois (John) Muzik of Alexandria, and Lola William
2 CONC son of Rock Falls, Ill. Margaret was preceded in death by her parents and two brothers, James and David.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may go to Lanesboro Cemetery and the United Methodist Church in Lanesboro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be one hour before the service on Saturday, July 31, 2010, at the United Methodist Church in Lanesboro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnson-Riley Funeral Home of Lanesboro is handling the arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary and photo from Rochester Post Bulletin, July 28, 2010.
