2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary E. Mindrum, 92, of Lanesboro, passed away on her birthday Wednesday, September 21, 2022 at her home in Lanesboro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Eleanor Nelson was born September 21, 1930, in Lanesboro to Willie "Bill" and Bertha (Gates) Nelson.
2 CONT
2 CONT She grew up in Lanesboro and worked for Hanson's Drug Store while she was in high school.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary graduated from Lanesboro High School in 1948.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1950 she married Caryl F. Mindrum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary worked for General Electric and the Post office where she retired from.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary enjoyed reading, watching the MN Twins, playing cards and board games.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Lanesboro American Legion Auxiliary, the Sunshine Club, and United Methodist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is preceded in death by her husband, Caryl; 2 sons, William, and Michael Mindrum; granddaughter, Adria Mindrum; daughter in-law, Judith Mindrum; 3 brother, James, Robert (Marlene), and David (Janice) Nelson; 4 sisters, Jean (A
2 CONC lan) Bremseth, Margaret Nelson, Lois (John) Muzik, Lola (Ken) Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT A private family burial with committal service will be held at Lanesboro Cemetery. Memorials are preferred to Lanesboro Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnson-Riley Funeral & Cremation Service is assisting the Mindrum family with arrangements.
