1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/33769067/david-alfred-nelson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral for David Alfred Nelson will be at 1 p.m. Saturday at Bethlehem Lutheran Church in Lanesboro, with Pastor Michael Smith officiating. Spring burial will be in Lanesboro Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Nelson, 66, of Lanesboro, died Monday (Feb. 9, 2009) at his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Aug. 23, 1942, in Lanesboro, he graduated from Lanesboro High School in 1960. On Aug. 31, 1963, he married Janice Asleson at Root Prairie Lutheran Church in rural Fountain.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a maintenance supervisor for the Fillmore County Highway Department for 38 years, a former member of the United Methodist Church Council, and a retired member of the Lanesboro Fire Department. He was also actuary of the Lan
2 CONC esboro Cemetery, a member of the United Methodist Church and the Preston Masonic Lodge, and a former member of the Lions Club, LHPA, the Community Club, and RRSR. Mr. Nelson enjoyed hunting and fishing, going to auctions and flea 
2 CONC markets, and antiquing. He also loved going to northern Minnesota to see all the wildlife, but most of all loved his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife; a brother, Robert (Marlene) of Watford City, N.D.; six sisters, Jean Bremseth of Houston, Margaret Nelson, Mary Mindrum and Ruth (Jim) Ostrem, all of Lanesboro, Lois (John) Muzik of Alexandria, Minn., a
2 CONC nd Lola Williamson of Rock Falls, Ill.; and many nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his parents, Willie and Bertha (Gates) Nelson; a brother, James; and three brothers-in-law, Allen Bremseth, Caryl Mindrum and Kenneth
2 CONC  Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be from 5 p.m. to 8 p.m. Friday at the Lanesboro United Methodist Church, and an hour before the service Saturday at Bethlehem Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family requests memorials to the United Methodist Church or Lanesboro Cemetery.
2 CONT
