1 NOTE
2 CONT Brenno - Clara
2 CONT Clara Brenno, 91, of Canton, died July 3, 2004 at Green Lea Manor Nursing Home in Mabel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clara Clarissa Ramlo was born Aug. 21, 1912, in Hesper, Iowa to James and Johanna (Bjorgan) Ramlo. She graduated from Hesper public school. She married Orval Lemont Brenno on Dec. 17, 1930, and they started farming in Lenora in 19
2 CONC 31. They lived there seven years. He preceded her in death. She lived at Green Lea Manor Nursing Home in Mabel the past two years. She was a member of Henrytown Lutheran Church. She was active in Ladies Aid, Ruth Circle and Strawb
2 CONC erry Fest Food Committee. She taught Sunday school for 25 years. She volunteered at Green Manor for 27 years, serving the lunch cart every Sunday afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include a son, Cleon (LaDonna) of Canton; six grandchildren; 11 great-grandchildren; a step-great-grandchild; a great-great-granddaughter; three step-great-great-grandchildren; and a sister, Myrtle Carpenter of Winona.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by two brothers and four sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral for Clara Brenno was July 6 at Henrytown Lutheran Church in rural Canton, with Minette Stalheim Johnson officiating. Burial was in the church cemetery. Mengis Funeral Home in Mabel was in charge of arrangements.
