1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/140997110/amy-catherine-ramlo
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Amy was born to Arne and Karen (Carlson) Arneson. She attended Alden Country School. She moved to Hettinger in 1930. On June 26, 1936, Amy was united in marriage to Harry Raymond "Ray" Ramlo at Hettinger. They worked in the defens
2 CONC e factories in WW II. In 1946 they returned to Hettinger, where they operated the Texaco Station and she ran a laundrey service for many years. Ray passed away on June 5, 1985.
2 CONT She is survived by a son Wallace (Wally), daughter in law, Dorla and three grandchildren: Scott, Joni, and Barbara.
