1 NOTE
2 CONT Earl Ramlo, 60, of Mabel, MN, died Tuesday November 17, 1981 at his home.  He was born November 25, 1920 in the town of Canoe, Winneshiek County, Iowa to Clarence and Lena (Bakken) Ramlo.  On March 6, 1941 he married Lucille Gunde
2 CONC rson in Locust, Iowa.  He had been a farmer in the Mabel area all his life.  He also was employed by the Winneshiek County Agricultural Stabilizaation and Soil Conservation office in Decorah for seventeen years and had been a memb
2 CONC er of the Winneshiek County ASCS Committee for the past three years.  He also had been the manager of the Mabel Mill and Elevator.
2 CONT Survivors are his wife; two daughters, Mrs. Lois Liudahl of Minneapolis and Mrs. Dale (Joyce) Gross of Atlantic, Iowa; five grandchildren; and two sisters, his twin, Mrs. Veneda Brown of Santa Ana, CA and Mrs. Phyllis Clapp of Ced
2 CONC ar Rapids, Iowa.  He was preceded in death by one brother.  Services were held on Friday November 19, 1981 at 1 p.m.  in the Hauge Lutheran Church, the Rev Gerhard Brase officiated and burial was in the Mabel, Cemetery.  Friends c
2 CONC alled at the Mengis Funeral Home, Mabel November 19 after 2 p.m. and at the church on Friday from noon until the service.
