2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT VENEDA BROWN OBITUARY
2 CONT Brown, Veneda Maxine (Ramlo)
2 CONT
2 CONT Veneda ("Toni") was born the elder to her twin brother, Earl, on Thanksgiving Day, November 25, 1920 in Winneshiek County, Iowa. Veneda and her family lived on the family farm outside of Decorah which had been established by her g
2 CONC randfather, Halvor Ramlo. Her parents were Betsy Olena (Bakken) and Clarence Ramlo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Veneda took a normal school education course allowing her to teach in a small one room county schoolhouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Robert H. Brown in Corpus Christi, Texas in March 1945. Robert later retired as a twenty year Marine Corps veteran. After his death in 1962 Veneda completed her college degree, received a California Teaching Credential
2 CONC , and earned a Masters Degree in Education.
2 CONT
2 CONT After teaching for one year in the Orange County School District she was promoted to Head Teacher equivalent to being Principal. She continued to work for a total of 22 years with the developmentally handicapped and retired from t
2 CONC he Orange County School District in August 1987.
2 CONT
2 CONT She continued with her hobbies of gardening and quilting until the end of her life. She enjoyed traveling to various states and countries with her family. She was proud to earn the title of "oldest lady" on her block (E. Avalon Av
2 CONC enue, Santa Ana).
2 CONT
2 CONT Veneda passed on November 6, 2014 just shy of her 94th birthday.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents; her husband, Robert H. Brown; her brothers, Orvin and Earl; her sister, Phylis; and by her two sons, Garry and Rex.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her daughter, Linda (Brown) Carne; grandchildren, Lisa Carne, Maria (and Chris) Lee, and Sam (and Elaine) Carne, Brittany Brown, and Vanessa (Brown) Melrose; great-granddaughters: Lillian and Courtney Lee, Becky
2 CONC  Sue and Ginnie Carne; and numerous nephews and nieces.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be conducted on December 12, 2014. She will join her husband, Robert, in the National Cemetery at Fort Rosecranz, Point Loma, California. In lieu of flowers, if you wish to make a donation, she would have preferred y
2 CONC ou choose the charity of your choice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by Orange County Register on Nov. 27, 2014.
