1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/243544867/forrest-andrew-folkedahl
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fillmorecountyjournal.com/forrest-folkedahl/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrest Folkedahl, age 78, of Hesper, Iowa, died Thursday, September 8, 2022, at St. Luke’s Hospital in Cedar Rapids, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrest was born on July 8, 1944, to Andrew and Nina (Nelson) Folkedahl. He attended school at Mabel and Spring Grove through the 10th grade. After that, he joined the Army on July 20, 1966, and served for two years. He met the lo
2 CONC ve of his life before he joined the service, and they were united in marriage on October 14, 1967. They lived in the Hesper-Mabel area their entire life and have resided at their current address since 1970.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrest had several jobs before working for Winneshiek County – Locust Shop as a road maintenance employee. He became the foreman of the crew and retired from that job in 2006 after 37.5 years for the county. He enjoyed fishing, c
2 CONC amping, playing cards, trading and upgrading several vehicles during his lifetime, and especially going to car auctions with his father-in-law Andy Sollien. His greatest joy was his family, especially spending time with his grandc
2 CONC hildren and three great-grandchildren. In his years after retirement, he took pride in keeping his lawn immaculate and his vehicles sparkling clean.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife of 54 years, Andrea Folkedahl (Hesper); daughter Brenda (Burt) Hongerholt, grandchildren  Kayla (Josh) Simiele, Christopher Hongerholt, and Kaia Hongerholt; great-grandchildren Addison, Vivienne, and Noa
2 CONC h; siblings Odis Fossum, Nanford (Karen Dehning) Folkedahl, and Lola (Robin) Foltz; brother-in-law Tim Sollien, and several nieces and nephews
2 CONT
2 CONT He is preceded in death by son Troy Folkedahl, brother Gene Folkedahl, sister Mavis Rilling, brothers-in-law John Fossum and Greg Nelson, and sisters-in-law Judy Folkedahl and Deb Nelson.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be 11 a.m. Wednesday, September 14 at the Hesper Lutheran Church in Hesper, Iowa, with the Rev. David Werges officiating.  Burial will be in the Hesper Public Cemetery.  Visitation will be from 4–7 p.m. Tuesd
2 CONC ay at the Hesper Lutheran Church in Hesper and one hour prior to services at the Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Filed Under: Obituaries
2 CONT Tagged With: Hesper, Mabel
