1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from the Compendium of Biography of Northern Minnesota dated 1902
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 969
2 CONT
2 CONT Nels H. Lofthus resides in Sletten township, Polk Co., Minnesota. Mr. Lofthus was born in Numedal, Norway, July 28, 1852. He was the oldest child and only son of four children born to Hellik and Berget (Kjome) Lofthus. The family 
2 CONC emigrated to America in 1867.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Lofthus was married in 1880 to Miss Margaret Henderson. Of this marriage nine children were born, namely, Carl H., Bernhard A., Martin, Tina, Albert, Nellie, Mabel, George, and Edwin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nels H. Lofthus, residing on section 30, in Sletten township, is one of the pioneer settlers of Polk Co., MN., and during his residence there has become well known as a progressive agriculturist and a man of exceptional business a
2 CONC bility. He has earned his way to the front by his hard labor and honest dealings and well merits his success and the esteem in whick he is held. Mr. Lofthus was born in Numedal, Norway, July 28 1852. He was the oldest chld and onl
2 CONC y son of four children born to Hellik and Berget (Kjome) Lofthus. The family emigrated to Americain 1867, settling in Clayton Co., Iowa. A year later they removed to Winneshiek Co., and a short time afterward made a permanent home
2 CONC  in Winnegabago Co., where our subject was reared and educated. He attended the common schools several winters and became familiar with the English language. In the spring on 1882 he fitted up a prairie schooner and after journeyi
2 CONC ng twenty-six days landed in Polk Co., with his family and all his perosnal property. He remained about a year at Fertile, with his brother-in-law, meanwhile looking over the Red River Valley, and visited North Dakota. About a mon
2 CONC th prior to the opening of the reservation he "squatted" on the land which he now owns. He has given much attention to stock farming, and has confidence in the dairy interests of Minnesota. He lived in a log house iln the early da
2 CONC ys and patiently awaited the coming of the railroad to that region. For about three years he had control of a country store at Sletten, which was established in 1895. In March, 1901, he and his son established a general storte at 
2 CONC Buzzle postoffice in Beltrami Co.. Mr Lofthus has met with success in his financial ventures and is classed among the prosperous men of his locality. Mr Lofthus was one of the organizers of Sletten township, and was one of the fir
2 CONC st to be elected jsutice of the peace. He has served as township clerk for over ten years, and takes active and commendable part in all local affairs. He is a Republican politically, and is a member of the Lutheran Church. Mr Loft
2 CONC hus married in 1880 to Miss Margaret Henderson. Of this marriage ten children have been born, namely; Carl Helmer, Bernhardt A., Martin/Nellie (twins), Tina, Albert Nelson, Nellie, Mabel, George, Edwin.* Reference: [https://www.fi
2 CONC ndagrave.com/memorial/125895162/niels-hellikson-lofthus Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 7 2020, 9:49:05 UTC''
