1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Woman, 88, dies in house fire
2 CONT
2 CONT An 88-year-old town of Deerfield woman died Friday night after rescuers pulled her from a fire in her home on Nuland Road.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carrie Berge was pronounced dead at St. Mary's Hospital, said Dane County Deputy Coroner John Stanley. The cause of her death had not been determined.
2 CONT
2 CONT Firefighters were called to Berge's home, about three miles south of the village of Deerfield, about 4:45 p.m. after her greatgrandson, 6, spotted flames, said Sgt. Gordon Disch of the Dane County Sheriff's Department. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berge's son, Arnold, and his wife, Janet, lived upstairs in the farmhouse and Carrie Berge lived below, said Deerfield Fire Chief Jeff Halverson. Apparently, Carrie Berge was the only one inside, he said.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halverson said the blaze appears to have started in the kitchen. Carrie Berge was in an adjacent room.
2 CONT
2 CONT The home was uninhabitable after sustaining smoke and fire damage, he said. Damage was estimated at more than $100,000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berge, Carrie S. DEERFIELD - Carrie S. Berge, age 88, died Friday, December 6, 1991 In a Madison hospital after a fire at her home. She was the former Carrie Spllde, born In Deerfield on March 10, 1903, the daughter of Nels and An
2 CONC na Spllde. On May 26, 1928, she married Arthur Berge and, together, they farmed for many years In the Town of Deerfield. She was a member of the Deerfield Lutheran Church, ELCW, and the Friends Group. Surviving Is a son, Arnold (J
2 CONC anet) Berge of Deerfield, two grandsons, Gary (Dawn) of Montello, and Dennis (Rhonda) of Deerfield; seven great-grandchildren; two brothers, Alfred Spllde of Madison/Harllngen, Texas, and Russell (Daisy) Spilde of Hot Springs Vill
2 CONC age, Arkansas; and a sister, Grace, (John) Topercer of Glenvlew, Illinois. Several nieces, nephews, grandnleces and grandnephews also survive. She was preceded In death by her husband In 1987; three sisters, Julia Engelstad, Norma
2 CONC  Feggestad, and Mildred Bluhm; and seven brothers, Norman, Knute, Lewis, Clarence, Helmer, Eugene, and George. Funeral services will be held on Tuesday, December 10, 1991 at 11:00 am. at the DEERFIELD LUTHERAN CHURCH, with Reveren
2 CONC d Floyd Olsen officiating. Burial will be In Deerfield Lutheran Cemetery. Friends may call at the funeral home In Deerfield from 4:00 p.m. until 8:00 p.m. on Monday, December 9, 1991. In lieu of flowers, memorials may be made to t
2 CONC he Deerfield Lutheran Church Kitchen Fund.
