1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Engelstad, Julia B. CAMBRIDGE -Julia B. Engelstad, age 92, of Cambridge, died on Wednesday, July 15, 1987,' at the Skaalen Home, Stoughton. She was born June 9, 1895 In the town of Deerfield the daughter of Nels and Anna (Knutson)
2 CONC  Spilde. She married Bendle Engelstad on June 11, 1919 In St. Paul's Liberty Church, and he preceded her in death on December 14, 1974. She was a Cambridge and Deerfield resident all of her life, was a member of Grace Lutheran Chu
2 CONC rch, Cambridge and Its Mary Circle. Survivors include two sons, Roger and Glenn, Cambridge; a daughter Mrs. Alice (Wells) Smith, Grand Haven, Michigan; seven grandchildren; three great-grandchildren; four brothers, Knute Spilde, M
2 CONC inneapolis, Minnesota, Alfred Spilde, Madison, Russell Spilde, Hot Springs Village, Arkansas, and Eugene Spilde, Copper Lake, Montana; and three sisters, Carrie Berge, Deerfield, Grace Topercer, Glenview, Illinois, and Norma Fegge
2 CONC stad, Madison. Funeral services will be held at '11:00 a.m. on Friday, at Grace Lutheran Church, Reverend Alfred H. Langhough officiating. .Burial In St. Paul's Liberty Cemetery. Friends may call from 4:00 until 8:00 p.m. on Thurs
2 CONC day, at the NITARDY FUNERAL HOME, Cambridge, and after 10:00 a.m. Friday, at the church.
