1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT George Spilde, Construction Foreman, Dies DEERFIELD - George B. Spilde, 64, lifelong Deerfield resident, who retired in 1972 as a construction foreman for the Findorff COnstruction Co., Madison, where he had been employed for 32 y
2 CONC ears, died Sunday night in Methodist Hospita, Madison, after a long illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Deerfield in 1909, he was a son of the Mr. and Mrs. Nels Spilde.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Navy veteran of the Pacific Theater in World War II, and was a member of the Deerfield American Legion and VFW Posts. He was married on May 28, 1936, to Maybelle Vethe of Deerfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Spilde was also a member of St. Paul's Liberty Lutheran Church, rural Deerfield, and the Deerfield Volunteer Firemen.
