1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gordon L. Monsen, 77, a former president of Monsen-Chicago Inc., a typography company founded by his grandfather in 1887, died Friday in Good Shepherd Hospital in Barrington. He was born in Chicago and moved to Bar
2 CONC rington in 1956. He co-authored "Photo-Mechanics and Printing " with Joseph Mertle and helped invent the color computator, a color-matching machine. Survivors include his wife, Mary Lynn; two sons, Robert and Gordon L. Jr.; a daug
2 CONC hter, Alisa M. Krost; a sister; and a grandchild. Services will be at 7:30 p.m. Wednesday in the Barrington Methodist Church, 311 S. Hough St., Barrington.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-369620184/gordon-leigh-monsen-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 18 2018, 11:47:3
