1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [swain.ftw]
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts about this person:
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial June 14, 2000 Cemetary at St. Paul's Liberty Lutheran Church-Deerfield Wisc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism December 23, 1923
2 CONT
2 CONT Engelstad, Doris A. CAMBRIDGE - Doris A. Engelstad, a life-long resident of Deerfield/ Cambridge, died on Saturday, June 10, 2000, at the age of 76. She was born on November 8, 1923, the daughter of Carl and Agnes Mickelson. As a 
2 CONC member of the Women's Army Corps, she served in the U.S. Armed Forces from 1944 until 1946. She belonged to the American Legion (Draeger/Fencil Post 260) and was a charter member of the Women's War Memorial Foundation, Washington 
2 CONC D.C. On May 7, 1950, Doris married Roger W. Engelstad, a former high school classmate. They worked together at the Deerfield Creamery, where she was employed as an accountant from 1947 until her retirement in 1970. Subsequently, t
2 CONC hey worked the Engelstad farm for more than 30 years. Doris was particularly known for her craft skills, includine painting, rosemaling, and especially hardanger, a Norwegian embroidery. Over the years, she was an active member of
2 CONC  St. Paul's Liberty Lutheran Church, participating in the Altar Guild, Hope Circle, and quilting for Lutheran World Relief. She is survived by her husband of 50 years, Roger; a daughter, Roxann Engelstad; a sonin-law, Edward Lovel
2 CONC l; sisters-in-law and brothers-in-law, Betty Mickelson, Alice and Wells Smith, Shirley and Glenn Engelstad; and many nieces, nephews, and cousins. She was predeceased by her parents; a sister, Cora; and brothers, S'ajiford, Edward
2 CONC , and Jerome. Visitation will take place on Tuesday, June 13, 2000, from 5:00 p.m. until 8fQO p.m. at OLSON-HOLTZHUTER-CRESS FUNERAL HOME, De"erfield. Funeral services will be held at 11:00 a.m. on Wednesday, June 14, 2000, at ST.
2 CONC  PAUL'S LIBERTY LUTHERAN CHURCH, Deerfield.
