1 NOTE (Rene)  Ole emigrated alone in 1868 to Quebec, Canada, and later to Goodhue County, MN and Rugby, ND.     The Iowa census (Winnebago county, Norway township)  of 1880 has Ole, (age 41) and Anna (age 23) with two children, Martin E
2 CONC . (age 1) and Carl Alfred, (age 2½, b. March, 1880).  The Iowa census of 1885 lists Ole as a laborer living in Worth County, Brookfield township, Section 3, the SE¼ of the NE¼. The 1895 census lists Ole and Anna and their 6 childr
2 CONC en farming in Logan township, Winnebago county, IA. Records at Forest City, county seat of Winnebago County, IA, show that Ole M. Knutson and wife Anna owned land in section 14 of Logan township. They bought it November 7, 1890, a
2 CONC nd sold it April 28th, 1897.
