1 NOTE The 1875 census for Bath Township, Freeborn County  in Minnesota lists John M. Knutson and his extended family:  John M. Knudson, 36; Anna H. Knudson, 21; Clara T. Knudson, 1; (brother) Olaus Knudson, 28, (father) Knut Knutson, 65
2 CONC ; (mother) Anna Knutson, 69; and (brother) Casper Knutson, 29.  John and his family are not listed on either the 1870 or the 1880 census of Bath Township. John's older brother, Lars, moved here in 1869-70, and this must have been 
2 CONC the reason that John came here.  John appears to have moved to Bath Township after June of 1874, as daughter Clara Taime is not on the county or church records as being born there, although the census record listing her as aged 1 
2 CONC in 1875 says that she was born in Minnesota.  John appears to have left Bath Township before 1878, because Karolina, born August, 1878 is not listed in Freeborn County or Church parish records.  John M. Knutson is listed on the to
2 CONC wnship plat of 1878, (40 acres, the SW 1/4 of the NE quarter, section 7), but there is no record of property bought or sold by him, so he may have rented for about 3 years. John's and Lars' homes were about 10 miles north of Alber
2 CONC t Lea, 4 miles apart.
2 CONT       His parents, who had been living with him, bought property near Fertile, IA., and they along with Casper and Olaus moved there, while John moved to North Dakota.  From the Pierce County, ND register of deeds office, the foll
2 CONC owing Morkve's or Morque's homesteaded there: Hans, John, Annie, Knute O., Susie, Ole, and Nels. Numbers are 153-72, 153-72, 153-73, 153-73, 154-72, 154-73, 154-73.
