1 NOTE
2 CONT Spring Grove Herald - April 17, 1941 - Mrs. Louisa Askelson passed away at Spring Grove Sunday, April 6, 1941 after a long illness. Louisa Bidne was a daughter of Mr. and Mrs. John Bidne and was born in Highland township January 5
2 CONC , 1869.  She was baptized and confirmed in Big Canoe Lutheran Church of which she remained a member all her life.  On March 22, 1894 she was married to Mons Askelson.  They established their home on the Askelson farm in Highland t
2 CONC ownship which styill is the family home.
2 CONT She is survived by the following children--Arthur and Walter at home; Lena (Mrs. Alfred Anderson) and Ida (Mrs. Meyer Sacquitne) both near Decorah, IA; Knut of Spring Grove; Maude of Minneapolis; Selmer of Highland twp. and Ruth (
2 CONC Mrs. Leon Johnson) of Lansing, IA.  She is also survived by seventeen grandchildren and the following brothers and sisters:  Peter J. and Ole J. Bidne of Highlandville; Mrs. Catherine Bidne of Decorah; Julia Bidne, Seattle, Washin
2 CONC gton and Mrs. Josie Vigen of Highland twp.  Her parents, husband, two brothers and a sister preceded her in death.
2 CONT Funeral services were held on Wednesday April 9, 1941 at the P. J. Bidne home in Highlandville and the Big Canoe Lutheran Church. Interment was in the Big Canoe cemetery, Rev. Wm. Hexom officiated.
