2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21718961/eline-siverson Memorial] - FindAGrave
2 CONT
2 CONT The link above refer to an obituary in Spokane Chronicle newspaper (Spokane, Washington), Friday Nov 3. 1911, page 2:
2 CONT
2 CONT WAS PIONEER OF SPOKANE COUNTY
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ellen Severson, Aged 72, Dies at Daughter's Home
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ellen Severson, aged 72 years, a pioneer of Spokane county, died Thursday night at the home of her son-in-law, Policeman Jacob Warner, E 709 Pacific avenue, after an illness of six weeks. Death was caused by a complication of
2 CONC  diseases.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Severson and her husband moved to Spokane county 28 years ago and made their home on a farm near Mica peak, southeast of Spokane. She resided there until eight years ago, when the family moved to Spokane.
2 CONT
2 CONT She leaves four sons - Randolph, Seigle, Nelson and Martin Severson - and two daughters - Mrs. Jacob Warner and Mrs. Albert Steffer - and eight grandchildren, all residing in Spokane.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will be held Sunday afternoon at 1 o'clock from the church at the Mica Peak cemetery. Interment will be at that place beside the grave of her husband, who died five years ago, and a daughter who died two years ago.
