0 @N6000000003875565190@ NOTE Minnesota Certificate of Death
1 CONT Number: 1943-MN-013367
1 CONT County: Rice
1 CONT Date: August 16, 1943
1 CONT "Minnesota Posten" newspaper obituary:
1 CONT Johannes O. Litsheim was born in Voss, Norway, August 6, 1863, of M B. Litsheim and Anna Magnesdatter Vethe. He came to USA when he was 18 years old and worked on rural farms in Iowa and Wisconsin. J. O. attended Luther College in
1 CONC  Decorah, Iowa, for one year, and then at Capital University and finally he enrolled as a student of theology at the Northfield Seminary, where he was graduated as a Candidate of Theology in 1888. Up until this time, he had also d
1 CONC one some teaching in Norwegian Parochial Schools in Lutheran Congregations.
1 CONT Rev. Litsheim accepted a call to serve a Norwegian parish in Jamestown, Kansas, and two years later he was a pastor at Madison, Minnesota. It has been recorded that he was the principal promoter in establishing the Norwegian Norma
1 CONC l School at Madison in 1892, which was thereupon operated by the United Lutheran Church as a institution for the training of Norwegian Parochial School teachers.
1 CONT Mr. Litsheim was twice married. His first wife was Ingebor Marie Thoe, who died in 1887. His second wife was Ingeborg Strand On account of poor health, this gentleman was forced to discontinue the holy ministry and therefore spent
1 CONC  the later part of his life in farming and as a rural mail carrier. His death occurred in 1943.
1 CONT "Kenyon (Minnesota) Leader" obituary - August 27, 1943
1 CONT John O. Litsheim was born in Voss, Norway, on August 6, 1863. He came to America when he was 18 years old. He attended school at Luther College in Decorah, Iowa, and graduated from St. Olaf College at Northfield. He was united in 
1 CONC marriage to Christine Strand in 1889 at Cannon Falls, Minnesota. 
1 CONT In 1905 the family moved to Kenyon and he lived here until he retired as rural mail carrier.
1 CONT He was preceded in death by three daughters, Inga, Annetta, and Agnes. He is survived by his wife Christine; six sons, Edward of Fairbanks, Alaska; Theodore of Nisland, South Dakota; Carl of Worcester, Massachusetts; Lt. Earl Lits
1 CONC heim of Camp Atterbury, Indiana; Obert of Fort St. John, Canada; and Robert of Kenyon. Also surviving are five Daughters, Christine (Mrs. George Bates) of Minneapolis; Theresa (Mrs. Walters) of Beverly Hills, California; Selma (Mr
1 CONC s. Whitmore) of Palermo, North Dakota; Anna (Mrs. Hiram Broin) of Kenyon and Doris (Mrs. Gibson) of Minneapolis.
1 CONT He passed away at Northfield, Minnesota, on Monday morning, August 16, 1943, at the age of 80 years and 10 days.
1 CONT Funeral services were held on Friday afternoon at the Hauge church. Rev. S. O. Simundson, who had known the deceased for 51 years officiated at the service. Mrs. Enoch Thune sang two songs during the services, "I Heard the Voice o
1 CONC f Jesus Say" and "Behold a Host Arrayed in White."
1 CONT Pallbearers were: Ludvig Iverson, Adolph Charlson, John E. Wallaker, Emil Rud, P. L. Golden, and Ole Hylie. Interment was in the Kenyon cemetery.
1 CONT Relatives from away were: Mr. and Mrs. John Gibson and family; Mrs. Christine Bates; Miss Corinne Gibson; Mrs. Obert Litsheim and son; Mrs. Edward Litsheim, all of Minneapolis; Mrs. Ben Whitmore of Palermo, North Dakota; Pvt. Luve
1 CONC rne Bates from South Caroline; Mrs. Albert Becker of St. Paul; Mrs. W. W. Gibson and daughter, Mabel, of Northfield; Supt. and Mrs. T. J. Litsheim and daughter of Nisland, South Dakota; and John Olson of Zumbrota. Lt. Earl Litshei
1 CONC m on maneuvers in Tennessee, was unable to get here until Saturday.
1 CONT Per article from Marcy Guild:
1 CONT Litsheim, Johannes Olsen
1 CONT Born Aug 6, 1863, at Voss, Bergen, Norway. 
1 CONT Attended Voss Teachers' Training School, 1879-81.
1 CONT Immigrated, 1881.
1 CONT Teacher, farmer, clerk in store, 1881-83.
1 CONT Teacher, Spring Prairie, Wisconsin, 1884.
1 CONT Attended Luther College, 1884.
1 CONT Capital University, 1885-86.
1 CONT Northfield Seminary, 1886-88 (C.T.)
1 CONT Pastor, Jamestown, Kansas, 1888-90; Madison, Minnesota, 1891-93.
1 CONT To Norway, 1893.
1 CONT Lived at Kenyon, Minnesota, 1894-1943.
1 CONT Parochial teacher and rural mail carrier.
1 CONT Ingeborg Marie H. Thoe 1886 (died 1887). Married Ingeborg Strand 1888.
1 CONT Facts about this person:
1 CONT Burial August 21, 1943
1 CONT Kenyon, Goodhue, Minnesota
1 CONT Emigration 1881
1 CONT Religion 
1 CONT Lutheran
1 CONT Nationality 
1 CONT Norwegian
1 CONT Nickname 
1 CONT John
